        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Toyota Owners 400, Federated Auto Parts 400, Daytona Speedweeks\n- Organizations: Crown Royal, Diageo, Seagram, Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series\n- Places: Richmond Raceway, Richmond, Virginia\n- Concepts: race title sponsorship, essay contest\n\nFacts:\n- In 2000, Diageo acquired Crown Royal when the Seagram portfolio was dissolved.\n- Crown Royal is a blended Canadian whisky owned by Diageo.\n- From 2007 to 2011, Crown Royal, a former title sponsor of the Toyota Owners 400, named the race after the winner of an essay contest during Daytona Speedweeks.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is an annual Monster Energy NASCAR Cup Series stock car race held at Richmond Raceway in Richmond, Virginia.\n- The Federated Auto Parts 400 is the second of two Richmond Raceway Cup Series races each year, with the Toyota Owners 400 held in the spring as the first race.",
